  {
   "line": 8,
   "text": "The cut filter's response is the step, smeared by that hump: slide it along, and add up what's still on the pass side. When the hump touches the cliff, the lobes past it are left out, and they add up to minus nine percent. Oh, so a hundred and nine is left. A longer rectangle just narrows the lobes, so the share stays.",
   "clip": "/Users/cleiton.loiola/personal/dsp-lessons/10-fir-windows/4-video/vo/line08.wav",
   "at": 88.25,
   "start": 88.25,
